Mon Nov  2 16:33:22 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Upgrade to version 3.5.11
  * Key Enhancements
    + CONJ-1386: New sslMode=allow: verify-full when the server
      announces TLS, unencrypted otherwise
    + CONJ-1353: Generate a CycloneDX 1.6 SBOM meeting CISA 2026
      minimum elements
    + CONJ-1356: Parsec authentication without BouncyCastle on Java
      8/11 and without provider-dependent key derivation
    + CONJ-1355: Add NonRegisteringDriver so DataSources and pools
      never register the driver in DriverManager
    + CONJ-1348: Reassembling packets larger than 16 MB copied the
      accumulated content once per fragment
  * Issues Resolved
    + CONJ-1387: LOAD DATA LOCAL INFILE file check must not match
      text inside identifiers or literals (CVE-2026-119210,
      bsc#1289117)
    + CONJ-1383: Connection init rebuilds
      session_track_system_variables from @@global, discarding
      session-level last_gtid set by MaxScale
    + CONJ-1379: Set explicit session tracking list and guard
      character_set_results like character_set_client
      (CVE-2026-119281, bsc#1289110)
    + CONJ-1381: Bound server-declared lengths by packet before
      reading from them (CVE-2026-119277, bsc#1289115)
    + CONJ-1382: Bound server-declared lengths by packet before
      allocating (CVE-2026-119276, bsc#1289116)
    + CONJ-1380: Rogue server can crash client during
      caching_sha2_password authentication (CVE-2026-119278,
      bsc#1289114)
    + CONJ-1357: XA recover() must not trust server-supplied
      gtrid_length/bqual_length (CVE-2026-119280, bsc#1289030)
    + CONJ-1374: Redirect URL password partially logged when
      containing '@'
    + CONJ-1372: caching_sha2_password full authentication fails
      over Unix socket when SSL is disabled
    + CONJ-1360: Incorrect dependency check in
      AwsIamCredentialPlugin
    + CONJ-1358: Client-side query timeout thread cannot be stopped
      and outlives an idle driver
    + CONJ-1352: Batched statements fail when trigger produces a
      result set
    + CONJ-1351: Reading invalid DATE value might throw unchecked
      exceptions instead of SQLException
    + CONJ-1346: Log-and-throw antipattern: server errors and
      hostname verification failures logged at DEBUG instead of
      WARN/INFO
    + CONJ-1345: DatabaseMetaData#getURL() exposes database password
      since Connector/J 3.5.10
    + CONJ-1344: DatabaseMetaData imported/exported keys ignore
      lower_case_table_names when using SHOW CREATE TABLE
    + CONJ-1343: DatabaseMetaData.getSQLKeywords() includes eight
      pairs of concatenated words
    + CONJ-1349: DatabaseMetaData.getBestRowIdentifier() returns
      primary key columns in an undefined order
- Changes of 3.5.10:
  * Key Enhancements
    + CONJ-1333: Add maxAllowedPacket connection option
    + CONJ-1339: Add maxAllowedColumns option to bound
      server-announced column count
    + CONJ-1330: Add infer test to CI
  * Issues Resolved
    + CONJ-1332: Reject multipart (>16 MB) packets before
      authentication to prevent pre-auth OOM from rogue server
    + CONJ-1342: socketFactory option allows loading arbitrary
      bytecode via jar: URL, enabling RCE when JDBC URL is
      attacker-controlled
    + CONJ-1307: Connection.setReadOnly(true) still allows DML
      statements to execute
    + CONJ-1326: Unsafe escaping in
      enquoteLiteral()/enquoteNCharLiteral()
    + CONJ-1327: Align SSL hostname verification with TLS libraries
    + CONJ-1329: LOAD DATA LOCAL INFILE validation fails open when
      bound parameter cannot be rendered
    + CONJ-1331: trustStore-configured TLS connections defer
      certificate chain/identity validation instead of validating up
      front
    + CONJ-1340: SQL injection via unescaped identifiers in
      updatable ResultSet generated statements
    + CONJ-1341: MariaDbPoolDataSource.getConnection(user, password)
      ignores user argument when pool password is supplied
    + CONJ-1328: restrictedAuth allowlist is matched with substring
      contains() instead of equality
    + CONJ-1338: Validate length-encoded integers fit non-negative
      int before use as length (CVE-2026-119279, bsc#1289111)
    + CONJ-1336: Regression CONJ-1282: TLS connection fails when
      JDBC hostname is absolute FQDN ending with trailing dot
    + CONJ-1335: getGeneratedKeys() throws integer overflow after
      batch insert when auto-increment value exceeds
      Integer.MAX_VALUE and returns bulk generated keys out of batch
      order
- Changes of 3.5.9:
  * Key Enhancements
    + CONJ-1223: Cache TLS trust/key managers across connections to
      reduce SSL connection cost
    + CONJ-1314: Add SPI for interactive dialog (PAM) authentication
      callback
    + CONJ-1311: Add dedicated option useIpForKillQuery for query
      cancellation
    + CONJ-1310: Add full native image support and CI coverage
  * Issues Resolved
    + CONJ-1320: PAM (dialog) authentication must require secure
      connection
    + CONJ-1319: Use constant-time comparison when validating server
      certificate fingerprint
    + CONJ-1318: Enforce allowLocalInfile=false on server
      local-infile request to prevent rogue server reading client
      files
    + CONJ-1322: Match local infile filename case-sensitively
    + CONJ-1323: LOAD LOCAL INFILE validation rejects statements
      preceded by line comments
    + CONJ-1315: Cap BigDecimal/BigInteger string parsing length to
      prevent CPU exhaustion if MitM
    + CONJ-1317: Ensure non-UTF8 charset cannot be used for protocol
      exchanges
    + CONJ-1304: CallableStatement parameter metadata read from
      mysql.proc, with MySQL info_schema fallback
    + CONJ-1299: Keep VALUES literals after last placeholder when
      rewriting batches
    + CONJ-1313: Race condition in HaMode#getAvailableHostInOrder
      can cause NPE
    + CONJ-1311: Connection.cancelCurrentQuery fails with
      SslMode.VERIFY_FULL when client socket IP is set
    + CONJ-1264: Handle LocalDateTime as zoneless wall-clock value
    + CONJ-1316: Pin Locale.ROOT on locale-sensitive call sites and
      date/time/Duration text formatting
    + CONJ-1324: Fix SQL parser to correctly handle '--' in
      expressions and reset lastChar after block comments
- Changes of 3.5.8:
  * Issues Resolved
    + CONJ-1305: XAResource.isSameRM() incorrectly returns true when
      rewriteBatchedStatements differs between connections
    + CONJ-1303: Statement.cancel() fails to kill running query
      during result streaming
  * Other
    + CONJ-1298: Performance improvement: avoid decoding extended
      format
- Changes of 3.5.7:
  * Key Enhancements
    + CONJ-1282: Added TLS SNI (Server Name Indication) support
    + CONJ-1271: Added MariaDbDataTruncation exception that includes
      MariaDB error code and error message
  * Issues Resolved
    + CONJ-1291: Fixed ConnectionPoolDataSource incompatibility and
      connection leaks due to internal ConnectionEventListener in
      Connector/J 3.5.x
    + CONJ-1286: Fixed MariaDbPoolPinnedConnection thread-safety
      issue
    + CONJ-1283: Fixed rewriteBatchedStatements bug when having
      parenthesis after VALUES parts
    + CONJ-1287: Fixed authentication plugin multi-exchange prefix
      (0x01) handling introduced in MDEV-37554
    + CONJ-1290: Fixed NullPointerException in
      MultiPrimaryReplicaClient
    + CONJ-1295: Fixed MariaDbClob compilation with JDK 26+
- Changes of 3.5.6:
  * Key Enhancements
    + CONJ-1238: rewriteBatchStatements implementation
    + CONJ-1274: Server prepared statement client failover to client
      prepared statement
  * Issues Resolved
    + CONJ-1278: Prepared statement caching enablement correction,
      same as 2.x
    + CONJ-1279: Metadata table name addition for 12.1 after
      MDEV-28933
    + CONJ-1280: Permit having multiple commands with initSql option
    + CONJ-1276: Connection#isValid(int timeout) does not obey
      passed timeout if network is down
- Changes of 3.5.5:
  * Issues Resolved
    + CONJ-1265: Ensure rollback and release savepoint operation are
      sent to server, even when no transaction is in progress
    + CONJ-1270: forceConnectionTimeZoneToSession does not always
      set timezone to server
- Changes of 3.5.4:
  * Key Enhancements
    + CONJ-1261: Added caching option for loadCodecs results to
      improve performance
  * Issues Resolved
    + CONJ-1234: Fixed incorrect type definitions in
      DatabaseMetaData.getTypeInfo()
    + CONJ-1247: Resolved potential race condition causing
      NullPointerException
    + CONJ-1250: Avoid redundant queries for
      CallableStatement.getParameterMetaData()
    + CONJ-1251: Fixed SSL configuration issue where zero SSL
      settings only functioned without explicit SSL configuration
    + CONJ-1252: Resolved GSSAPI authentication error when server
